{
  "tool": "fractions-ratio",
  "owner": "FIT Site",
  "version": "2026-10-18",
  "tolerance": {
    "rel": 1e-06,
    "abs_when_expected_zero": 1e-09,
    "note": "numbers relative 1e-6 (7 s.f.), zero absolute 1e-9; integers (numerators, denominators, terms, n, indices), strings, booleans, nulls, lists and error objects exact; errors {error: schema class, reason: lower_snake_case} (KAT_SCHEMA 17:46)"
  },
  "calc_module": "lib/sims/families/fractions-ratio.calc.js",
  "convention": "Module FITCalcRatio (lib/sims/families/fractions-ratio.calc.js); op = function name, fields exactly as the family prompt. Fractions are {num, den} integers, |value| <= 1,000,000 (continued_fraction 1e9); results in lowest terms with den > 0 (sign on num), 0 = 0/1. mixed = {whole, num, den} with 0 <= num < den for results >= 0, null for negative results. compare result is '<', '=' or '>' for a vs b; difference = a - b. Ratios: 2-6 positive integer parts. ratio_unchanged: the quantity at unchanged_index keeps its value, the other quantity changes by the signed 'change'; before:after part ratios given; MathError ratios_inconsistent when the two ratios are equal, no_positive_solution when any amount <= 0. proportion kinds direct y=kx, inverse y=k/x, square y=kx^2, inverse_square y=k/x^2, sqrt y=k sqrt(x). map_scale 1:n with map lengths in cm, real in km and km^2 (null when the map input is omitted). percent_change percent = (new - original)/|original| x 100. reverse_percent original = final/(1 + p/100). compound A = P(1 + r/(100 m))^(m t), per_year m default 1. gp: r = 1 gives S = na; sum_infinity only when |r| < 1 (else null, converges false). gp_terms_to_exceed: least n with S_n strictly greater than target (a, r > 0). telescoping: sum_{k=1}^{n} 1/((k+p)(k+q)), 0 <= p < q integers, A = 1/(q-p), B = -A. mix: alligation, fraction_a = (c_b - t)/(c_b - c_a). best_buy: lowest price per unit, ties to the lowest index. continued_fraction: Euclidean-algorithm terms with the floor convention (a0 may be negative, later terms positive; with more than one term the last is at least 2), convergents [p, q]. cf_sqrt: a0 and the shortest repeating period (perfect square -> period [], is_square true). best_approximation: closest p/q with 1 <= q <= max_den (ties to the smaller q), approx_error = value - p/q (named approx_error so it is never read as an error object). egyptian: greedy (Fibonacci-Sylvester) with exact integers; a denominator above 2^53 - 1 -> RuntimeError denominator_too_large. mediant (a+c)/(b+d) in lowest terms.",
  "oracle": "script-verified textbook formulae (Singapore primary and secondary mathematics; H2 Mathematics series; Hardy and Wright, An Introduction to the Theory of Numbers; Khinchin, Continued Fractions). Builder = hand-written integer gcd arithmetic, closed-form series, Euclid continued fractions, the periodic surd algorithm, Fraction.limit_denominator, ceiling-division greedy; check() = fractions.Fraction, sympy solve/summation/apart/continued_fraction_periodic, brute-force denominator search, term-by-term sums and loop compounding.",
